1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:05,350
Well, I must say, Leonard,

2
00:00:05,350 --> 00:00:08,310
when I first heard your idea for Giant Jenga,

3
00:00:08,310 --> 00:00:10,360
I was skeptical.

4
00:00:12,570 --> 00:00:13,610
I can't blame you--

5
00:00:13,610 --> 00:00:16,330
Tiny Twister was a complete bust.

6
00:00:16,330 --> 00:00:17,780
No, I was wrong.

7
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:19,940
The looming threat of

8
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:22,640
being crushed under a pile of lumber

9
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:25,350
does add a certain spice.

10
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:28,020
I've never felt so alive.

11
00:00:32,530 --> 00:00:34,060
Oh, hello, Alex.

12
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:36,370
Uh, let me go get you last night's recordings.

13
00:00:36,380 --> 00:00:37,490
What recordings?

14
00:00:37,490 --> 00:00:40,100
Well, you remember when you told me I talk in my sleep?

15
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:42,800
Well, it occurred to me that, like most things I say,

16
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:45,100
it's probably pure gold.

17
00:00:45,330 --> 00:00:47,470
So I started recording it all,

18
00:00:47,470 --> 00:00:49,940
and now Alex gets to comb through eight hours

19
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:53,230
of what I like to call "Sheldon After Dark."

20
00:00:53,790 --> 00:00:55,160
- Hey, Leonard. - Hey.

21
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:56,860
Just playing a little Giant Jenga here.

22
00:00:56,860 --> 00:01:00,110
Oh, I know-- I'm the one who had to buy him the helmet.

23
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:02,650
So, do you have any plans this weekend?

24
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:04,840
Well, most of Saturday's gonna be figuring out

25
00:01:04,840 --> 00:01:06,490
where to put this game when we're done.

26
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:08,310
How about you?

27
00:01:08,310 --> 00:01:09,600
Oh, I'm gonna go see Kip Thorne

28
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:12,110
give a lecture on subatomic space-time.

29
00:01:12,710 --> 00:01:14,910
That's his take on John Wheeler's quantum foam.

30
00:01:14,910 --> 00:01:16,050
That should be great.

31
00:01:16,050 --> 00:01:17,890
Well, if you want, you can come with me.

32
00:01:17,890 --> 00:01:20,500
Ah, I'd love to, but I'm supposed to hang out with Penny.

33
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:21,620
Well, bring her.

34
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:24,140
Well, she's not really into that kind of stuff.

35
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:25,640
Yeah, okay.

36
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:27,100
Well, if you want to hear about the lecture,

37
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:28,680
I can tell you all about it at work,

38
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:31,040
or, you know, over dinner sometime.

39
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:32,800
What?

40
00:01:36,030 --> 00:01:38,620
Jenga, I win!

41
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:08,550
Oh, come on, that can't be true.

42
00:02:08,550 --> 00:02:11,260
I did the research-- Tony the Tiger,

43
00:02:11,260 --> 00:02:12,750
Dig'em the Frog, Cap'n Crunch,

44
00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:14,810
Toucan Sam, Count Chocula,

45
00:02:14,810 --> 00:02:18,210
Trix the Rabbit, Snap, Crackle and Pop.

46
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:21,620
Not one cereal mascot is a girl.

47
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:25,770
It's a total breakfast sausage fest.

48
00:02:26,950 --> 00:02:27,960
Are we done with this?

49
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:30,760
Almost-- Franken Berry, Boo Berry,

50
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:32,870
Sugar Bear and the Honey Nut Cheerio bee,

51
00:02:32,870 --> 00:02:35,310
I believe his name is Buzz.

52
00:02:36,190 --> 00:02:37,110
Terrific.

53
00:02:37,110 --> 00:02:39,230
Something weird happened and I don't know what to do about it.

54
00:02:39,230 --> 00:02:40,120
What's going on?

55
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:42,800
Sheldon's assistant asked me on a date last night.

56
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:44,290
How could you do that to me?

57
00:02:44,290 --> 00:02:47,280
You know I've been working it with Alex for weeks.

58
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:49,390
Working it? You can't even talk to her.

59
00:02:49,390 --> 00:02:51,740
I talk with my eyes.

60
00:02:58,600 --> 00:02:59,600
You look like my little cousin

61
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:02,220
when he's dropping one in his diaper.

62
00:03:02,710 --> 00:03:04,830
She knows I have a girlfriend.

63
00:03:04,830 --> 00:03:06,590
It's so weird.

64
00:03:06,590 --> 00:03:08,610
Oh, my God. You're loving this.

65
00:03:08,610 --> 00:03:10,210
To my bones.

66
00:03:11,950 --> 00:03:14,270
I mean, I'm not gonna do anything about it. I love Penny.

67
00:03:14,270 --> 00:03:16,700
It's just nice to have a young, attractive woman

68
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:18,400
sniffing around the goods.

69
00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:21,880
I both hate you and want to be you.

70
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:24,730
This is Ryan Gosling all over again.

71
00:03:24,730 --> 00:03:26,620
Aw, gentlemen.

72
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:29,380
What is on the conversational menu this morning?

73
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:31,170
Leonard stole my woman, and he knew full well

74
00:03:31,170 --> 00:03:34,270
I was only six to eight months away from making my move.

75
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,010
I didn't steal anyone.

76
00:03:37,010 --> 00:03:38,890
Your assistant is totally hitting on this jerk

77
00:03:38,890 --> 00:03:40,180
and he loves it.

78
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:42,560
Well, that's not acceptable.

79
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:44,130
I'm her boss.

80
00:03:44,130 --> 00:03:46,430
She needs to be solely focused on my needs,

81
00:03:46,430 --> 00:03:48,480
not distracted by your pasty,

82
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:51,120
androgynous brand of sexuality.

83
00:03:53,010 --> 00:03:54,660
I'm androgynous?

84
00:03:54,660 --> 00:03:56,140
Oh, please. Look at you

85
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:58,690
with your pouty bee-stung lips.

86
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:01,580
What do you guys think I should do?

87
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:04,430
I say you tell Alex your heart belongs to Penny,

88
00:04:04,430 --> 00:04:06,090
I provide her a shoulder to cry on,

89
00:04:06,090 --> 00:04:08,970
and then roughly half a year later I give it to her good.

90
00:04:12,010 --> 00:04:15,460
I want to thank you all for coming on such short notice.

91
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:17,460
Uh, in the past, I've reached out

92
00:04:17,460 --> 00:04:19,540
to each of you individually,

93
00:04:19,540 --> 00:04:22,220
but I believe my present situation

94
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:25,220
requires the collective wisdom of the group,

95
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:28,510
which as you can see from your commemorative T-shirts

96
00:04:28,510 --> 00:04:30,340
I have dubbed

97
00:04:30,340 --> 00:04:34,050
Sheldon Cooper's Council of Ladies.

98
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:37,690
What is happening?

99
00:04:38,370 --> 00:04:43,290
I need your advice about a delicate workplace situation.

100
00:04:43,290 --> 00:04:45,020
Uh, to protect those involved,

101
00:04:45,030 --> 00:04:47,130
I'll be changing their names.

102
00:04:47,130 --> 00:04:48,490
Who's involved?

103
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:51,860
Well, a short, bespectacled colleague of mine

104
00:04:51,870 --> 00:04:55,580
who lives in the shadow of his brilliant roommate.

105
00:04:55,590 --> 00:05:00,450
Let's call this colleague Ricardo Shilly-Shally.

106
00:05:01,390 --> 00:05:02,710
You're talking about Leonard.

107
00:05:02,710 --> 00:05:06,480
No, no, Shilly-Shally has red hair

108
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:10,270
and, uh, he briefly served in the Mexican Navy.

109
00:05:12,870 --> 00:05:16,360
Anyway, despite the fact that he has a girlfriend,

110
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:18,890
Shilly-Shally has been the recipient

111
00:05:18,890 --> 00:05:22,580
