112
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:25,250
- It's your assistant Alex, isn't it? - No.

113
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:30,790
Not... No. This is Tondelaya Della Ventimiglia.

114
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:33,810
Wait, what the hell's going on with Leonard and Alex?

115
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:36,650
I'm sorry. Who's talking about Leonard and Alex?

116
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:40,640
Fine. Ricardo and Tondelaya.

117
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:43,470
Okay, look, it's not really about Ricardo and Tondelaya.

118
00:05:43,470 --> 00:05:46,300
It is really about her boss,

119
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:48,770
who doesn't quite know how to handle this situation

120
00:05:48,770 --> 00:05:50,440
and could use your advice,

121
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:55,070
which is surprising because Dr. Einstein Von Brainstorm...

122
00:05:56,210 --> 00:05:58,650
He's usually pretty smart about these things.

123
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:01,100
I'm gonna kill her.

124
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:02,400
I'm sure you've got nothing to worry about.

125
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:04,140
Leonard would never cheat on you.

126
00:06:04,140 --> 00:06:05,250
She's right.

127
00:06:05,250 --> 00:06:06,810
But say the word-- I got a lab

128
00:06:06,810 --> 00:06:10,290
full of cocaine-addicted monkeys with nothing to lose.

129
00:06:11,370 --> 00:06:13,950
One of them could end up in the backseat of her car.

130
00:06:14,670 --> 00:06:16,560
Or her shower.

131
00:06:18,070 --> 00:06:19,190
Ladies, ladies, please.

132
00:06:19,190 --> 00:06:21,070
We're not here to talk about Penny, okay?

133
00:06:21,070 --> 00:06:22,500
We're here to talk about me.

134
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:25,860
Uh, I mean Einstein Von Brainst... Oh, darn it!

135
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:28,450
All right, I guess the cat's out of the bag.

136
00:06:28,450 --> 00:06:30,100
Let me explain what's going on--

137
00:06:30,100 --> 00:06:31,580
Ricardo is really Leonard...

138
00:06:31,580 --> 00:06:34,020
We know what's going on, Sheldon!

139
00:06:34,900 --> 00:06:36,650
Well, what should I do?

140
00:06:36,650 --> 00:06:38,520
Well, Alex is your employee.

141
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:40,910
If she's doing something that's making Leonard uncomfortable,

142
00:06:40,910 --> 00:06:42,470
you should talk to her.

143
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:44,030
Oh, no, he's not uncomfortable at all.

144
00:06:44,030 --> 00:06:45,340
No, he's loving it.

145
00:06:45,340 --> 00:06:47,950
Yeah, he's strutting around like he's five-foot-six.

146
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:51,170
What... He's loving it?

147
00:06:51,170 --> 00:06:53,330
Sheldon, you need to talk to Alex right away.

148
00:06:53,540 --> 00:06:55,450
Talk to her? That's all you've got?

149
00:06:55,460 --> 00:06:58,370
With a cool name like Sheldon Cooper's Council of Ladies,

150
00:06:58,380 --> 00:07:00,250
I really expected more.

151
00:07:00,810 --> 00:07:02,610
Give me back the T-shirts.

152
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:15,650
Alex...

153
00:07:15,650 --> 00:07:16,900
check my schedule.

154
00:07:16,900 --> 00:07:18,960
What does my afternoon look like?

155
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:20,650
I think it's pretty wide open.

156
00:07:20,650 --> 00:07:23,550
Oh, wait. Here's something at 4:00.

157
00:07:23,550 --> 00:07:26,390
"Give Alex a talking to"?

158
00:07:27,690 --> 00:07:29,910
Well, that snuck up on us, didn't it?

159
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:32,050
Is there a problem?

160
00:07:32,050 --> 00:07:34,190
Let's not call it a problem.

161
00:07:34,190 --> 00:07:36,380
Let's call it an opportunity.

162
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:39,060
To solve a serious problem.

163
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:40,600
What did I do?

164
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:43,300
You don't know? Oh, you poor dear.

165
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:45,630
Your ovaries are squirting so much goofy juice

166
00:07:45,630 --> 00:07:48,150
into your brains you don't even know which way is up.

167
00:07:50,710 --> 00:07:53,950
You made an inappropriate sexual advance

168
00:07:53,950 --> 00:07:56,470
- towards Dr. Hofstadter. - What?

169
00:07:56,470 --> 00:07:59,430
I didn't make a sexual advance on anybody.

170
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:01,740
Now, there's no need to get defensive.

171
00:08:01,740 --> 00:08:04,260
I'm not unsympathetic to your plight.

172
00:08:04,270 --> 00:08:07,490
My father used to say that a woman

173
00:08:07,490 --> 00:08:12,400
is like an egg salad sandwich on a warm Texas day.

174
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:15,430
What?

175
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:19,860
Full of eggs and only appealing for a short time.

176
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:23,560
This conversation is making me uncomfortable.

177
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:25,180
Yeah, you and me both, sister.

178
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:26,310
Now,

179
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:29,320
please understand...

180
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:32,880
I don't hold you responsible for your behavior

181
00:08:32,890 --> 00:08:35,050
because, see, from an evolutionary standpoint,

182
00:08:35,060 --> 00:08:37,970
you're a slave to your desire to reproduce.

183
00:08:37,980 --> 00:08:39,760
But during the work day,

184
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:43,050
when you feel possessed by amorous intent,

185
00:08:43,050 --> 00:08:45,100
may I suggest that you suppress it

186
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:47,950
by leafing through this illustrated book

187
00:08:47,950 --> 00:08:50,340
of sexually transmitted diseases?

188
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:52,750
Let's see here. Oh, yes.

189
00:08:52,750 --> 00:08:55,000
Check out this oozy doozy.

190
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:58,790
I have to go.

191
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:00,130
So does this fellow,

192
00:09:00,130 --> 00:09:03,010
but he can't without it burning like hot soup.

193
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:11,090
Hey, pretty lady.

194
00:09:12,270 --> 00:09:14,010
Oh, you seem extra happy.

195
00:09:14,010 --> 00:09:15,010
Uh, I guess I am.

196
00:09:15,010 --> 00:09:16,680
Any particular reason why?

197
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:18,760
Mm, I don't know, just having a good day.

198
00:09:18,770 --> 00:09:20,830
This morning Sheldon fell asleep on the way to work,

199
00:09:20,830 --> 00:09:21,800
so I got to listen to the radio--

200
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:23,260
that was pretty crazy.

201
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:26,150
Anything else?

202
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:28,180
I found this quiz online called

203
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:29,610
"Which Star Trek Character Are You?"

204
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:32,910
and it only took me four tries to get Captain Kirk.

205
00:09:32,910 --> 00:09:34,410
That's great.

206
00:09:34,410 --> 00:09:37,390
Oh. It. Was.

207
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:41,420
Well, I'm glad you're having such a great day.

208
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:43,820
And the one thing that could make it even better

209
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:45,990
is an evening with my special girl.

210
00:09:45,990 --> 00:09:47,160
Oh, and who's that?

211
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:48,830
What do you mean?

212
00:09:48,830 --> 00:09:51,460
Oh, I just didn't know if you meant me or Alex.

213
00:09:51,470 --> 00:09:53,520
Um, why would I mean Alex?

214
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:54,730
Because I know she hit on you

215
00:09:54,730 --> 00:09:56,860
and I know you liked it!

216
00:09:56,860 --> 00:09:58,920
What...?

217
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:03,880
Don't play dumb with me, Ricardo Shilly-Shally!

218
00:10:09,690 --> 00:10:12,030
I'm missing something.

219
00:10:13,350 --> 00:10:16,320
Did you say something to Penny about Alex?

220
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:20,160
Oh, yes. Yeah, and a fat lot of good it did me.

221
00:10:20,160 --> 00:10:22,970
All she did was get mad at you.

222
00:10:24,090 --> 00:10:25,840
Why would you do that?

223
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:27,950
I needed advice about a woman.

224
00:10:27,950 --> 00:10:29,130
I would have asked you,

225
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:31,420
but if the last few years have proven anything,

226
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:34,090
it's that you can't tell a uterus from a unicycle.

227
00:10:35,590 --> 00:10:37,460
At least I know not to blab to a girl

228
00:10:37,460 --> 00:10:39,870
about somebody flirting with her boyfriend.

229
00:10:39,870 --> 00:10:41,530
Good to know.

230
00:10:41,530 --> 00:10:43,080
Yeah, a few more helpful hints like that,

231
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:45,920
you may find yourself on the Council of Ladies.

232
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:47,560
Hello.

233
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:50,610
I see.

234
00:10:50,610 --> 00:10:52,520
Uh, what time?

235
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:54,320
Very well, then.

236
00:10:55,450 --> 00:10:58,920
That was the Human Resources Department at the university.

237
00:10:58,920 --> 00:11:02,480
Apparently, my assistant Alex has filed a complaint

238
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:05,890
accusing me of inappropriate behavior in the workplace.

239
00:11:05,890 --> 00:11:08,610
Oh, my God, what did you do?

240
00:11:08,610 --> 00:11:10,840
Hmm, let me think.

241
00:11:11,910 --> 00:11:14,420
Nothing. I'm a delight.

242
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:24,240
Human Resources Department.

243
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:26,210
Human Resources Department.

244
00:11:26,210 --> 00:11:28,080
Human Resources Department.

245
00:11:28,900 --> 00:11:30,550
Come in.

246
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:32,720
Hello.

247
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:34,800
Ah, Dr. Cooper, have a seat.

248
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:36,070
Thank you.

249
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:38,330
I called you in today because your assistant

250
00:11:38,330 --> 00:11:40,970
Alex Jensen has lodged a complaint against you.

251
00:11:40,970 --> 00:11:42,360
So I've been told.

252
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:45,310
But I can't understand what she has to complain about.

253
00:11:45,310 --> 00:11:48,880
I mean, she has a front-row seat as I make scientific history.

254
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:51,370
There's string cheese in my mini-fridge,

255
00:11:51,370 --> 00:11:53,590
and that's for anyone.

256
00:11:53,590 --> 00:11:55,250
Yeah, and just yesterday

257
00:11:55,250 --> 00:11:58,510
I led her away from a life of sexual promiscuity

258
00:11:58,510 --> 00:12:02,590
by making her look at pictures of disease-ridden genitalia.

259
00:12:08,470 --> 00:12:10,970
Cancel my next appointment.

260
00:12:10,970 --> 00:12:13,070
This is gonna take a while.

261
00:12:13,070 --> 00:12:14,350
Dr. Cooper,

262
00:12:14,350 --> 00:12:15,920
you said things to your employee

263
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:18,580
that you just cannot say in the workplace.

264
00:12:18,580 --> 00:12:20,220
Like what?

265
00:12:20,220 --> 00:12:21,850
Well, according to Ms. Jensen,

266
00:12:21,850 --> 00:12:25,430
you said that she was a slave to her biological urges

267
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:29,590
and called her an "egg salad sandwich."

